92	Church of Syrena	t	22	3	The people of bloodhaven are mostly travelers living their lives in the skies and only stopping here briefly. Even those who make extended stays in Haven City live their lives under the constant threat of dangerous storms and wind while making their living trading with airmen. Overall the people of Bloodhaven have a deep respect, or fear, of the Sky Goddess Syrena. The temple the least poorly built structure in town, tall stone walls all lean outwards, the temple has a completely open roof allowing for optimal view of the sky. Inside the temple is a rowdy place full of excited travelers eager to leave an offering for the goddess and receive their sip of wine in return. Any funds raised by the church are committed to the upkeep of the town to ensure the ships keep coming and the wine keeps flowing. Just as the Goddess decreed. A small clergy have settled long term at the temple, sleeping under the stars in small beds. They are usually willing to allow travelers a night in the temple so long as they are reverent to the goddesses' boisterous ways. “A tithe must be paid and a toast must be raised.” 	Place	\N
1	Haversnippets	f	\N	2	Sed nec nibh porta, venenatis nulla in, facilisis odio. Etiam et tempus tellus. Donec et est commodo, sollicitudin tortor quis, laoreet nisl. Phasellus maximus dolor diam, sit amet vehicula ipsum tristique at. Suspendisse id risus lacus. Aenean ultrices libero purus, id malesuada lorem elementum sit amet. Vestibulum rhoncus, massa non feugiat tristique, enim est accumsan libero, quis cursus sapien nisl et est. Ut efficitur nisl sit amet tellus efficitur placerat. Proin ultricies, ante quis sollicitudin sollicitudin, turpis nibh tristique metus, ut auctor augue sem et massa. Sed tortor odio, euismod vitae convallis a, rutrum et metus.	Planet	\N
65	Port Galeton	t	43	30	<div>... A western coastal town of Damabrae which has a trade port maintained by mostly dwarves and dragonborn folk.</div>	Town	\N
42	Mara Cuora	t	41	30	<div>Mara Cuora (Heart-soul of the sea) is the fourth planet in the solar system of the Cragstar. Here you will find large ocean bodies and various continents spread throughout as well as towering mountains and deep underground valleys. Mara Cuora is home to a people who have lost their connection with their past. Records of history still rot in caves undiscovered, and those who live nearby show little interest. Ironically the soul of tradition lingers on as the general population is consumed with their daily rituals and family affairs. The gods only know what hidden power lies in the ancient records of yore.</div>	Planet	127
68	Pruost	t	43	30	<div>A coastal town in the south east of Damabrae, home to many gnomes and a few elves. This place reeks of magic.\n\nWhere the order of the starweavers was founded and maintained a headquarters.</div>	Town	\N
