61	Members	Draven Blackthorn: A mysterious and deadly assassin, Draven specializes in silent kills and covert operations. His loyalty to the Darkstars is unwavering, and he strikes fear into the hearts of their enemies. Malachite the Forsaken: A powerful sorcerer who was once an advisor to Lord Dramshire, but was banished to the Shadowplane. He seeks to return to Mara Cuora and unleash dark energy upon the land.\nValeria Shadowbane: An Elf sorcerer/warlock and former Arcane Scholar. Valeria possesses a telepathic connection with a mysterious entity and is determined to breach the magical barrier on Mount Va'aurum to access the dark energy and facilitate the Darkstars' return. She is charismatic, manipulative, and willing to sacrifice anyone who stands in her way. \nSeraphina Nightshade: A seductive and enigmatic sorceress, Seraphina uses her charms to manipulate others to do her bidding. Her mastery of illusions and mind control make her a formidable member of the Darkstars.\nKaelar the Bloodreaver: A fearsome warrior with a thirst for power, Kaelar wields a wickedly sharp blade and is known for his brutal fighting style. He revels in the chaos and destruction he brings to the enemies of the Darkstars.\nLyra Mistralis: A skilled archer and tracker, Lyra is the eyes and ears of the Darkstars. Her keen senses and unparalleled marksmanship make her an invaluable scout and reconnaissance specialist. 	\N	2023-05-25 20:11:55.430372+00	30	\N	\N	2	19
62	Plot	The Darkstars, driven by their malevolent ambitions, plot a sinister plan to return from the Shadowplane and disrupt the balance of light in Mara Cuora. Their ultimate goal is to darken all the powerful meridian portals scattered across the planet, effectively cutting off the divine light bestowed by the deities of Mara Cuora.\n\nBy extinguishing the divine light, the Darkstars aim to create a void that they can fill with their own twisted version of light. This false light would serve as a means for them to observe and control the inhabitants of Mara Cuora, shrouding the world in their nefarious influence.\n\nWith the meridian portals under their control, the Darkstars seek to harness the energies within them to empower their own dark magic and further their malevolent agenda. They plan to channel this corrupted energy into the very essence of Mara Cuora, corrupting its natural balance and plunging the world into darkness.\n\nThrough their manipulation of the portals and the severing of the connection to the deities' light, the Darkstars aim to establish their dominance over the planet and its inhabitants. They desire to reign as puppet masters, using their false light to surveil and control the lives of the people, ensuring their unwavering loyalty and obedience.\n\nThe return of the Darkstars and the implementation of their twisted vision would bring about a grim era for Mara Cuora, where true light and divine guidance are replaced by a perversion of illumination. It falls upon the heroes and defenders of the planet to thwart their plans, restore the balance of light, and protect the free will and autonomy of the inhabitants against the encroaching darkness.	\N	2023-05-25 20:18:39.789717+00	30	\N	\N	2	19
63	Plot	Aided by Orin, he plans to help summon each of the Darkstars back to Mara Cuora with the aid of the magical items which have been sent through the portals (meridian points) from each of the Darkstars as a talisman of communication with those who would listen.\n\nHe only has 3 right now. One for Valeria (the eye of shadows) for the meridian at Mt. Va'aurum.	\N	2023-05-25 20:26:22.981606+00	30	51	\N	2	\N
65	Abilities	Celestial Attunement: A Starweaver is deeply attuned to the celestial energies and can tap into the power of the stars. This connection allows them to infuse their spells and abilities with radiant or ethereal effects, enhancing their potency.\n\nStellar Sight: Starweavers possess enhanced vision in low light or darkness, being able to see clearly amidst starlit environments. They can discern hidden details and navigate through dimly lit areas with ease.\n\nCelestial Blessing: Starweavers can call upon celestial forces to bestow blessings upon themselves or their allies. These blessings augment their abilities temporarily, granting boosts to strength, agility, or magical prowess.\n\nCelestial Lore: Starweavers have access to celestial knowledge and can tap into cosmic insights. They can establish connections with celestial beings, seek guidance, and gain understanding of celestial prophecies or events.\n\nAstral Healing: Starweavers can harness celestial energy for healing purposes. They can accelerate the natural healing process, mending wounds and revitalizing themselves or others through the rejuvenating power of the stars.\n\nStarfall Barrage: Starweavers can summon a barrage of starlight projectiles that rain down upon enemies. These radiant projectiles burn and disorient foes while purging darkness and malevolent influences.\n\nCelestial Projection: Starweavers can temporarily project their consciousness into the celestial plane. This astral projection grants them the ability to traverse cosmic realms, commune with celestial entities, and gain access to hidden knowledge and divine insights.	\N	2023-05-28 14:35:59.441154+00	30	\N	\N	2	17
66	Background	Gauston Radiford, the curious Dragonborn fisherman from Port Galeton, first encountered Jorpus Materfeld during one of his fishing expeditions along the coast of Wystria. It was a day like any other, with Gauston casting his nets into the sea in search of a bountiful catch.\n\nAs Gauston hauled in his nets, he noticed a peculiar glimmering object caught amidst the fish. Intrigued, he reached down and retrieved a small, intricately crafted trinket. It emanated an aura of mystery and hinted at a deeper significance.\n\nUnbeknownst to Gauston, his discovery did not go unnoticed. Jorpus Materfeld, a renowned collector of rare items and a well-known figure in Wystria, had been keeping a watchful eye on the activities along the coastline. He had an uncanny ability to sense when something of value had been found, and Gauston's discovery had piqued his interest.\n\nIntrigued by the Dragonborn's find, Jorpus sought out Gauston, extending an invitation to meet and discuss the artifact further. Gauston, always open to new experiences and eager to learn, accepted the offer, curious to discover the true nature and significance of the trinket he had stumbled upon.\n\nTheir initial meeting proved to be a turning point in Gauston's life. Jorpus Materfeld, with his vast knowledge and network of connections, captivated Gauston with tales of lost civilizations, ancient magic, and the allure of rare and valuable treasures. Jorpus recognized Gauston's keen eye and natural talent for finding unique items, and he saw the potential in enlisting the Dragonborn as a collector for his personal pursuits.\n\nUnder Jorpus's mentorship, Gauston delved deeper into the world of rare artifacts and became an integral part of Jorpus's quest to amass a collection of extraordinary items. With each successful find, Gauston's relationship with Jorpus grew stronger, as they embarked on expeditions together, explored hidden locations, and unraveled the mysteries surrounding the artifacts they sought.\n\nHowever, as Gauston became more entangled in Jorpus's world, he began to notice subtle changes in his own demeanor and behavior. The fisherman's once carefree nature became tinged with an air of secrecy, and he found himself drawn to The Wyvern, a tavern frequented by Jorpus and his associates, at unusual hours.\n\nLittle did Gauston know that his involvement with Jorpus Materfeld would lead him down a path fraught with unforeseen consequences, as the line between curiosity and obsession blurred. The true nature of Jorpus's intentions and the impact of Gauston's discoveries would test his loyalty, integrity, and the very essence of his being.\n\nThus, Gauston's journey as a collector of rare items under Jorpus's guidance began, marking the start of a relationship that would challenge his perceptions, force him to confront his own transformation, and ultimately shape the fate of both Gauston and the artifacts he sought.	\N	2023-05-28 14:53:43.04049+00	30	64	\N	2	\N
