3	52	\N	Swarm Bats Large	Large Swarm of Bats\nLarge swarm of Tiny beasts, unaligned\n Armor Class 12\n Hit Points 66 (12d10)\n Speed 0 ft., fly 40 ft.\n\tSTR 5 (-3)\tDEX 15 (+2)\tCON 10 (+0)\n\tINT 2 (-4)\tWIS 12 (+1)\tCHA 4 (-3)\n\n\n\nSaving Throws —\n Skills Perception +3\n Damage Resistances Bludgeoning, Piercing, Slashing\n Condition Immunities Charmed, Frightened, Grappled, Paralyzed, Petrified, Prone, Restrained, Stunned\n Senses Blindsight 60 ft., passive Perception 13\n Languages —\n Challenge 2 (450 XP)Traits\nEcholocation. The swarm can’t use its blindsight while deafened.\nKeen Hearing. The swarm has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on hearing.\nSwarm. The swarm can occupy another creature’s space and vice versa, and can move through any opening large enough for a Tiny bat. The swarm can’t regain hit points or gain temporary hit points.\nBreak Apart. When the swarm is reduced to 33 hit points or fewer, it splits into two separate Swarm of Bats creatures. Each new swarm has half the remaining hit points (rounded down). They roll initiative immediately after splitting.Actions\nBites. Melee Weapon Attack: +4 to hit, reach 0 ft., one creature in the swarm’s space.\n Hit: 14 (4d6) piercing damage, or 7 (2d6) piercing damage if the swarm has half its hit points or fewer.\nOverwhelm (Recharge 5–6). The swarm moves up to its flying speed through the spaces of up to 3 creatures of its choice. Each creature must make a DC 13 Dexterity saving throw or take 14 (4d6) piercing damage and be blinded until the start of its next turn as the bats swirl around their head and body. On a success, the creature takes half damage and is not blinded.	f
4	52	\N	Fortune Telling	Your fortune told by Madam Eva:\n\nHistory: Knowledge of the ancient will help you better understand your enemy...\nA wounded elf has what you seek, he will part with it to see his dark drams fulfilled... a name?... Kasimir\n\nPower: A weapon of vengence, power and strength, a sword of sunlight.\nLook for a den of wolves overlooking a mountain lake. The treasure belons to Mother Night.\n\nProtection:  a powerful force for good and protection, a holy symbol of great hope.\nThis treasure lies in a dragon's house, in hands once clean and now corrupted.\n\n\n\nStrahd's Enemy One who will help you greatly in the battle against darkness, and is the key to victory\nEvil's favored bride is the one you seek. The one whom he loves above all others will be his downfall\n\nLocation Your enemy is a creature of darkness, whose powers are beyond mortality. This will lead you to him when you are ready.\nHe lurks in a hall of bone, in the dark pits of his castle.	t
5	52	\N	Castle Ravenloft: As You Know It	Castle Ravenloft is built on a 1000 ft spire of stone directly above Barovia villiage. It features a tall central spire and tall walls guarding a courtyard. There are many traps, secret rooms and hidden vaults, you have advantage and searches to find such after study of the model in the amber temple\n\n-Spire: Unvisited\n-upper floor 2: Unvisited\n-upper floor 1: Unvisited\n\n-Main floor: guarded by gargoyles Red dragon wyrmlings and more. Dinner hall and Chapel are here.\n\n- First Basement: The Hall of Bones (where you stole Argynvost's Skull) and Rahadins private study. (Map 11, 12)\n\n- 2nd basement the catacombs and dungeons (Secret tunnel) (Map 11, 12)	t
7	52	\N	Item: Sunsword of Skywarden Sergei	Sentient magic weapon recovered from the Werewolf cave containing a echoe of Segrei Von Zarovich, Strahd's Brother.\n\n+2 Magic Longsword, finesse \n\nBonus Action: activate/deactivate the blade in any shape the user wishes\n\nOnce Per day: The wielder gains fly speed equal to their walking speed for one minute while holding the sword.\n\n+1d8 radiant damage vs undead\n\nBlade emits bright light in a 15-foot radius and dim light for an additional 15 feet. The light is sunlight. While the blade persists, you can use an action to expand or reduce its radius of bright and dim light by 5 feet each, to a maximum of 30 feet each or a minimum of 10 feet each.	t
6	52	\N	Allies Against Strahd	------Team Backdoor------\nThe Vagabonds\nEsmerelda d"avnir\nX -Vasili Von Holst, Bard\n\n------Team Front door:------\n-20 Commoners from Barovia Village + Burgomaster Izmark \n-40 Commoners From Valaki + Warden Luvesh (vistani leader)\n-Rudolf Van Richten\n\n------Team Air Attack------\n-12 Vistai + Old Man Larry\n-6 dark elves\n-3 Wereravens (Danika, husband Urwin and eldest son)\n\n------Team Teleporer------\n-6 Werewolves  + Kiril (alpha)\n-The Lich Kazan + the blind elf Kasimir \n\n? - The Revenants + Godfrey Guillem and Vladomir\n? - The Golems from the tower\n? - Father Samel from St. Markovia’s abby and his mongrelfolk\n\n\nSet up aid station nearby:\n-3 Priests of St. Andral (Father Lucian and 2 alter boys)	t
13	115	\N	Ursaurians	A group of minotaur that was also one of the three major clans that sacked Paxxaria. Renowned warriors for their ferocity and guerilla tactics, the Ursaurians were a formidable force that even Legionaires were reluctant to engage. The Ursaurians are often attuned to nature, protecting it from more destructive forces while also acting a fierce protector. \n\nThe Ursaurians reside in the Southern Gallic forests, though they are one of the most wide-spread barbarian clans.	t
8	52	\N	Item: Holy Symbol of Ravenkind	Recovered form the mausoleum at Argynvostholt.\n\nWondrous item, legendary (requires attunement by a cleric or paladin of good alignment)\n\n"The Holy Symbol of Ravenkind is a unique holy symbol sacred to the good-hearted faithful of Barovia. It predates the establishment of any church in Barovia. According to legend, it was delivered to a paladin named Lugdana by a giant raven — or an angel in the form of a giant raven. Lugdana used the holy symbol to root out and destroy nests of vampires until her death. The high priests of Ravenloft kept and wore the holy symbol after Lugdana's passing."\n\nThe holy symbol is a platinum amulet shaped like the sun, with a large crystal embedded in its center. The holy symbol has \n\n----10 charges. It regains 1d6 + 4 charges daily at dawn.----\n\nHold Vampires. 1 charge\nAs an action, Present the holy symbol to make it flare with holy power. Vampires and vampire spawn within 30 feet of the holy symbol when it flares must make a DC 15 Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, a target is paralyzed for 1 minute. It can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns to end the effect on itself.\n\nTurn Undead. 3 charges\nIf you have the Turn Undead or the Turn the Unholy feature, present the holy symbol while using that feature. When you do so, undead have disadvantage on their saving throws against the effect.\n\nSunlight.  5 charges\nAs an action present the holy symbol to make it shed bright light in a 30-foot radius and dim light for an additional 30 feet. The light is sunlight and lasts for 10 minutes or until you end the effect (no action required).\n\nA glimmer of hope\nA creature wearing the symbol cannot be affected by Strahd's mind-altering abilities	t
9	52	\N	Item: The Tome of Strahd	Recovered from the coffin of Patrina, Kasimir's dead sister. \n--Note-- The book has been returned to Strahd\n\nReadable Excerpts:\n\nI am the Ancient. I am the Land. My beginnings are lost in the darkness of the past. I was the warrior, I was good and just. I thundered across the land like the wrath of a just god, but the war years and the killing years wore down my soul as the wind wears stone into sand. All goodness slipped from my life. I found my youth and strength gone, and all I had left was death. My army settled in the valley of Barovia and took power over the people in the name of a just god, but with none of a god’s grace or justice.\n \nI called for my family, long unseated from their ancient thrones, and brought them here to settle in the castle Ravenloft. They came with a younger brother of mine, Sergei. He was handsome and youthful. I hated him for both.\n \nFrom the families of the valley, one spirit shone above all others. A rare beauty, who was called “perfection,” “joy,” and “treasure.” Her name was Tatyana, and I longed for her to be mine.\n \nI loved her with all my heart. I loved her for her youth. I loved her for her joy. But she spurned me! “Old One” was my name to her—“elder” and “brother” also. Her heart went to Sergei. They were betrothed. The date was set.\n \nWith words she called me “brother,” but when I looked into her eyes they reflected another name: “death.” It was the death of the aged that she saw in me. She loved her youth and enjoyed it. But I had squandered mine. The death she saw in me turned her from me. And so I came to hate death—my death. My hate is very strong. I would not be called “death” so soon. I made a pact with death, a pact of blood. On the day of the wedding, I killed Sergei, my brother. My pact was sealed with his blood.\n \nI found Tatyana weeping in the garden east of the chapel. She fled from me. She would not let me explain, and a great anger swelled within me. She had to understand the pact I made for her. I pursued her. Finally, in despair, she flung herself from the walls of Ravenloft, and I watched everything I ever wanted fall from my grasp forever. It was a thousand feet through the mists. No trace of her was ever found. Not even I know her final fate. Arrows from the castle guards pierced me to my soul, but I did not die. Nor did I live.\nTatyana my beloved, why must you hurt me like you have. I feel you in my grasp, yet you escape me the moment we touch. She taunts me! She taunts me! What will it take for you to love to me? I can change, I know I can, but you have forced my hand generations ago. I will find a way. I must find a way.\nI have studied much since then. “Vampyr” is my new name. Everyone and everything is against me, even the sun. Little can harm me now, except for that damned sword Sergei brought with him. I must dispose of that awful tool, its sight alone causes me to feel and act in disparity. A possible solution to my now named curse could be to find a successor, yet none match my intellect or skill. Mother once told me a true king is only as good as the one he shares his throne with. I will find that person. They must relief me of my position. They must bring an end to this, so I can finally live the rest of my days in peace and quiet. \nOnce I felt true compassion, this has since that horrid day been replaced with a dull emptiness. I wish to love, yet my heart does not seem to warm, not even at the sight of my beloved, Tatyana. The word 'love' no longer has meaning to me and has been replaced with a similar hollowness. I no longer experience pleasure or passion, the things that once caused me to pursue my life have now turned against me.	t
10	52	\N	Ravenloft DM Map		f
14	115	\N	Ibanites	While Ursarians are a large contending force near the Southern Gallic Forests and the Southern Ibanite plains, the Ibanite Dwarves protect their domain within the Titan Mountains. They're also one of the few dwarves that have a prominent cavalry, contending with the Ursaurians and facing them on the open fields where their height failed them before. \n\nRiding Rams, Goats and Donkeys, the Ibanites were not easy to subdue when Paxxarian Legions marched into their lands.	t
11	115	\N	Paxxarians	Once the largest empire in the entire realm. The Paxxarians started from the hills of Lupin and first conquered the Brass Peninsulas then expanded their reach throughout the known world. While the Paxxarians lost the majority of their military might upon the collapse of the Empire, their influence sits in other dormant ways.\n\nPaxxarians are a human race from the warmer coasts of Lupin.	t
12	115	\N	Vandals	One of the great clans that overturned the Paxxarian Empire. When the Paxxarians couldn't recruit enough peasants for their legions, the senate turn to commissioning mercenary corps. The corps consisted of folks that wouldn't typically be allowed to join the Paxxarian Legions. However, the number of corps outnumbered the Paxxarian coffers. The Vandals and others marched to the capital of Paxxaria. The Senate refused to give in to the demands of the assembled corps, so the Vandals were the largest group that looted the capital.\n\nThe Vandals are a group of tieflings that have been at odds with the Paxxarians. Renowned warriors that dominate the mountainous region of Madania.	t
15	115	\N	Lombadites	In the Madanian Ridges, the Lombadite Dwarves use magic to create and carve new homes. Practicing arcane arts that descend from the stars, the Lombadites were often consulted for matters of divination or fate. Their temples are notoriously wealthy for all the patronage offered to them by Kings and Senators. The Lombadites shrewdly protect their wealth.	f
16	115	\N	Narsegians	To the northern White Cap Coasts, the Narsegians navigate the treacherous waters of the Gray Sea. Powered by runes and tattoos, the Narsegians are fierce warriors who survive the harshest conditions, groups constantly warring with each other and raiding coastal villages as the Paxxarians no longer keep the sea raiders at bay. The Narsegians are also renowned for their coveted Blacksmithing. Entire cities built as forges that build ships, enough weapons for ten armies and siege weapons that could topple entire empires.	t
17	115	\N	Galls	The Gallic Woods are a mixture of material and Fae Woods. While Ursaurians dominate the material wood, the Galls dominate the Gallic Faewoods. Able to blend in as moving trees, the Paxxarians attempted to exterminate the Galls' entire existence when they refused to bend the knee to Imperial rule. \n\nThe Galls are excellent in hunting, animal handling and most activities that involve survival in the harsh depths of the forests.	t
18	115	\N	Inglaterians	Renowned for the cavalry, the Inglaterrians ride in the northeastern woods and plains. While having a history of nomadic living, the Inglaterrians split off between those who settle in hilly stone castles and those who continue to built temporary wooden settlements then burn them as soon as they migrate. \n\nInglaterrians are a type of human that are prominent throughout the North.	t
