61	61	I speak in cryptic riddles to leave others guessing.	Absolutely nothing matters, why even bother.	I am being hunted by a vengeful spirit that I unwittingly angered.	I am paranoid and suspicious of those around me, even those who are trying to help.	Kreepaskardimal always liked to tinker but he never had any formal training, he somehow just knew how to put parts together. As he grew older he realized that the gadgets he was making hadn't been invented yet and the blueprints for them were gifts from the future, he began meditating and sought out the spirits to understand his strange visions and inexplicable, if somewhat faulty, knowledge of the future. He's been a medium ever since. \nHis visions have caused a great deal of trouble as they are not always accurate. Kreepaskardimal keeps to himself and puts on a flat neutral prosona and tends to expect the worst from everyone.	250	2	50	Grey	pale and wrinkly	Silvery		Spooky	True Neutral	a little gnome with squinty eyes. his hair is long and droops in front of his face always looking of into the distance and muttering to himself	Oh yes he has loads of allies though sometimes forgets who he's already made friends with.
33	33	When I set my mind to something, I follow through no matter what gets in my way.\n\nI'm confident in my own abilities and do what I can to instil confidence in others.	My purpose is everything.\n\nDetermined.	I have a family, but I have no idea where they are or if they're alive. One day, I hope to see them again.\n\nI carry my sword, and the book, and I carry them so that I will never forget my roots. I will never let them be taken away from me.	The people who destroyed my home will stop at nothing to see me caught or killed.\n\nI have trouble trusting in my allies. I distrust Gnomes even more.\n\n\nShort Tempered\nNo Nonsense	It's been a few years since you left your home.\n\nCultists came and ransacked your village, killing some and kidnapping many others. They came one night without warning, unprovoked. When they came to your home, your family had barricaded the door and prepared to fight, but your mother pulled you aside and told you you need to go. You tried to refuse, but she wouldn't let you.\n\nWhen you're mother hugged you for the last time, she handed you the family sword. She also gave you a small leather book, bound and locked. She told you never to try and open it, and to never tell anyone you had it. She said you would know what to do when the time was right.\n\nYou mother repeated, "Never open it until you are certain the time is right."\n\nAs she pushed you out the back window, the last thing you saw before escaping was a person taking off his mask, but his race was totally foreign to you. He spoke his orders in Gnomish. Around his neck was a necklace with the symbol of a triangle pointing down, three tear drops inside.\n\nSince then, you've kept the book secret, and tracked the cultists, learning skills in history and survival as you've made your way through the cities and wilderness, searching through libraries and caves alike. You've also learned Gnomish. You're only goal up to now has been to find your family.\n\nYour investigation has led you to the city of Ilmaterum.	19	Over 7ft	290lbs	Brown	Brown/Grey	pink(braided)	You have a twin sister, Laila, whom you hate because you believe she abandoned you.	Inheritor	Neutral Good		\N
