29	29	Ardryll is quick with a smirk, quicker with a joke, and fastest with his reflexes. He has an uncanny knack for diffusing tension with his sharp wit and an infectious laugh, yet he never lets his guard down. He displays an insatiable curiosity for the unknown and an irrepressible desire for adventure. Ardryll often talks to Whiskers in hushed tones as though discussing grand plans or important decisions. He can also be found casually flipping his parents' token whenever he's deep in thought, a habit that's left him with an uncanny knack for predicting coin tosses.\n	Despite his chaotic tendencies, Ardryll values freedom above all else - the freedom to choose his path, live his life, and be the master of his destiny. He believes that every creature deserves a chance at a free life, something that fuels his dedication to protecting the woods. His experiences have made him loathe injustice and oppression, leading him to sometimes take the law into his own hands, to the dismay of local authorities.\n	Ardryll's bond with Whiskers is stronger than most friendships; his little mouse companion is his confidant, partner in crime, and the family he once lost. His wooden token is not only a key to his past, but it also keeps him grounded in the present and guides him to the future. Ardryll also feels a deep bond with the woods that gave him refuge and purpose, making him a relentless defender against any who would threaten its peace.\n	For all his charms, Ardryll is notoriously unreliable when it comes to plans and promises. His chaotic nature makes him prone to distraction and whimsy, often leading to hasty, poorly thought-out decisions. He can also be a bit too free with his humor, making light of situations where seriousness is due, sometimes at the expense of others' feelings. This inability to comprehend boundaries and his resistance to discipline are some of the biggest obstacles he must overcome.	Tragedy struck Ardryll Camorock's life when he was a mere child, as his parents succumbed to a deadly plague that swept through their humble city home. Forced onto the streets, he quickly learned the harsh rules of survival in a city that cared little for the weak. His only solace was a pet mouse, Whiskers, and a small, intricately carved wooden token — his parents' last gift. The token, a miniature replica of a family emblem, served as a constant reminder of their love and of his roots. It also doubled as a useful lockpick in his increasingly creative methods of survival. As Ardryll aged, his longing for a different life took him to the outskirts of the city. He found solace in the woods, training to become a ranger, finding ways to blend his urban survival skills with his natural Elven affinity to the woods.	101	5'5"	120 lbs.	Green	Sun-kissed	Chestnut		Urchin	Chaotic Neutral	Standing at just over 5'5", Ardryll Camorock is on the short side for a wood elf, yet his slender frame belies his considerable strength. His sun-kissed skin hints at a life spent under the canopies, while deep green eyes echo the mysteries of the forest. A tangle of chestnut hair cascades over his shoulders, often hiding the multiple earrings of curious design. A scruffy beard lends him a rugged charm, a marked contrast to his meticulously maintained, city-street smart clothes. His most intriguing feature, however, is the constant companionship of a small, clever-eyed mouse perched on his shoulder or burrowed into a pocket, peeking out with curious whiskers twitching.	Having survived his years on the city streets, Ardryll became an unofficial member of the local thieves' guild, the "Silent Serpents". They respected his survival instincts and ability to slip into places unseen, although Ardryll always maintained a cautious distance from their more nefarious activities. In the forest, Ardryll befriended an eccentric hermit, Old Gnarlbark, who shared knowledge of the woods and its creatures, helping Ardryll transition from an urchin to a ranger. Among the woodland creatures, Ardryll is regarded as an ally, due in no small part to the diplomatic skills of his trustworthy emissary, Whiskers the mouse.
