23	23	Toma is a whimsical soul who marches to the beat of his own drum. He's curious to a fault, constantly seeking new knowledge and experiences. He has a jovial nature and often uses humor to diffuse tense situations. While he appears somewhat aloof and chaotic, Toma is deeply empathetic and has a knack for understanding others' feelings. He loves a good joke and can often be found trying to coax a smile from the sternest of faces. He also has an unyielding belief in the power of a well-cooked sarmale.	Above all, Toma values freedom and individuality. He believes everyone should be free to be themselves, regardless of societal expectations. He also values knowledge and sees magic as a tool for understanding the world. Despite his chaotic nature, Toma has a strong moral compass and will always stand up for those who can't protect themselves. He believes that with great power comes great responsibility, although he interprets this in his own unique, often unconventional, way.	Toma holds a deep bond with his pet bat, Brie, who he considers his closest friend and confidant. He also cherishes his relationship with his Solomonar mentor, seeing him as a father figure. Despite his wandering lifestyle, Toma is deeply connected to his hometown of Sighisoara and its people, and he carries a piece of it wherever he goes. He often sends back magical trinkets and absurd tales from his travels, much to the amusement and bemusement of the villagers.	Toma's biggest flaw is his unpredictability, both in his spellcasting and in his general behavior. He can be absent-minded and forgetful, often losing track of his belongings or getting lost in his own thoughts. His lack of discipline often results in magical mishaps, and he sometimes forgets the consequences his spells can have on those around him. Despite his good intentions, Toma's unconventional approach to magic can sometimes cause more harm than good.	Our tale begins in the quaint village of Sighisoara, nestled in the heart of Transylvania, where Toma was born under the most unusual circumstances. His mother, the village's renowned baker, always claimed Toma popped out of a loaf of cozonac, a traditional Romanian sweet bread, during a very intense baking session for the Easter holidays.\n\nGrowing up, Toma was always a little odd. He had a penchant for conversing with invisible entities, an affinity for pet bats which he named after various types of cheese, and a strange habit of dipping his sarmale (stuffed cabbage rolls) in raspberry jam much to the chagrin of his fellow villagers. However, it was his keen interest in the arcane and mystical that truly set him apart.\n\nToma's destiny was set in motion when a mysterious and eccentric old man visited Sighisoara. This man was a Solomonar, a member of an ancient Romanian order of weather-controlling wizards. The Solomonar was instantly intrigued by the peculiar boy and, after a brief yet intense staring competition with Toma's favorite pet bat, Brie, he decided to take Toma under his wing.\n\nUnder the Solomonar's tutelage, Toma quickly proved to be a prodigious wizard, despite his unusual methods. He developed a fondness for transmuting ordinary objects into farm animals, often leaving a trail of bewildered chickens, sheep, and the occasional cow in his wake. His spellcasting often went awry, frequently resulting in unexpected showers of mamaliga (polenta), a phenomenon that only served to reinforce his reputation as a rather eccentric character.\n\nHowever, Toma's most impressive ability was his talent for controlling weather. With a wave of his hand, he could summon a blizzard or clear a stormy sky. The only problem? Toma's weather spells were linked to his emotions, leading to sudden, uncontrollable changes in weather whenever he experienced strong feelings. A fit of laughter could result in a spontaneous snowfall, while a bout of sadness might call forth a thunderstorm. His hometown quickly adapted to these unpredictable weather patterns, always carrying an umbrella and a sunhat, just in case.\n\nToday, Toma the Peculiar wanders the world, seeking new magical knowledge and trying to gain better control of his emotions (and the weather). His journey is full of humorous mishaps, from accidentally turning a nobleman's trousers into a surprisingly aggressive goose, to causing a downpour of pickles in the middle of a grand ball. Despite the chaos he often causes, Toma remains good-hearted and earnest, always ready to lend a hand (or cast a spell) to help those in need.	28	6	150	Green	White	Black	\N	Hermit 	Chaotic Good	Toma is a tall, lanky figure with a shock of messy black hair and twinkling green eyes that dance with mischief. His skin is fair, speckled with a smattering of freckles across his nose and cheeks. A perpetually mischievous grin is usually present on his face, and he's rarely seen without his pet bat, Brie, perched on his shoulder. He dresses in somewhat mismatched clothing, favoring a brightly colored patchwork robe, a wide-brimmed hat adorned with feathers, and a pair of worn leather boots.	Toma's main ally is his pet bat, Brie, who he often converses with, much to the bewilderment of others. He also maintains ties with his mentor, the Solomonar, who still occasionally provides guidance and support from a distance. Toma has befriended many villagers and townsfolk along his travels, who appreciate his good heart despite his chaotic magic. Although he isn't part of any formal organization, Toma can often rely on a network of friends and acquaintances for help when needed. However, his unpredictability and oddities have also earned him a number of detractors, especially among those of a more serious or rigid disposition.
