682	Class	Reckless Attack	Starting at 2nd level, you can throw aside all concern for defense to attack with fierce desperation. When you make your first attack on your turn, you can decide to attack recklessly. Doing so gives you advantage on melee weapon attack rolls using Strength during this turn, but attack rolls against you have advantage until your next turn.	93
823	Class	Hybrid Transformation	At 3rd level you can focus your Ki and control your Lycanthropy, taking a chosen hybrid form. As an action you may spend 2 ki points to take a shape from the “Lycan Shapes Table” for 1 minute. If you are reduced to 0 hit points your transformation immediately ends and you fall unconscious. \n-Attacks made with your natural weapons, such as claws or teeth, count as unarmed attacks for you and do slashing damage.\n-Thickened Hide-\nIf you are not wearing armor your proficiency bonus is added to your armor class.\n-Primal Attacks-\nYour proficiency bonus is added to damage you do with unarmed attacks or monk weapons.\n-Consumption-\nWhen a medium or larger creature within 5 feet of you dies you may use your reaction to feast on their remains restoring 1 ki point. This cannot be activated if the creature is a construct, elemental, ooze, or undead.\n-Cursed-\nIf you start your turn with 0 ki points you must immediately make a DC 14 wisdom saving throw. On a failed save you must immediately move toward, and take the attack action against, the nearest creature friend or foe. You then regain control of your mind until the start of your next turn and can use bonus actions, remaining movement and reactions normally.	90
656	Class	Channel Divinity (1/rest)	At 2nd level, you gain the ability to channel divine energy directly from your deity, using that energy to fuel magical effects. You start with two such effects: Turn Undead and an effect determined by your domain. Some domains grant you additional effects as you advance in levels, as noted in the domain description.When you use your Channel Divinity, you choose which effect to create. You must then finish a short or long rest to use your Channel Divinity again.Some Channel Divinity effects require saving throws. When you use such an effect from this class, the DC equals your cleric spell save DC.Beginning at 6th level, you can use your Channel Divinity twice between rests, and beginning at 18th level, you can use it three times between rests. When you finish a short or long rest, you regain your expended uses.	91
